# `from` after `|` before an operator name: the fix removes it (DS0152).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | from where a > 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    ERROR@9..13
      IDENT@9..13 "from"
    WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
    WHERE_OP@14..25
      IDENT@14..19 "where"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      BIN_EXPR@20..25
        NAME_REF@20..21
          IDENT@20..21 "a"
        WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
        GT@22..23 ">"
        WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
        LITERAL@24..25
          LONG@24..25 "1"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0152]: `from` is not an operator
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | from where a > 1
  |          ^^^^ `from` starts a query; after `|` comes an operator
  |
  = help: remove `from` and pipe into `where`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where a > 1
which parses without errors
